cid.org/0009-0000-5927-9606", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Gerald", "family": "Versluis", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "297", "language": "en", "link": [{"URL": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/979-8-8688-3010-5.pdf", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/979-8-8688-3010-5", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 20]], "date-time": "2026-08-20T07:59:02Z", "timestamp": 1787212742000}, "score": 42.043236, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://link.springer.com/10.1007/979-8-8688-3010-5"}}, "subtitle": ["Connect AI Agents to Your .NET Applications with the Model Context Protocol"], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "ISBN": ["9798868830099", "9798868830105"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1007/979-8-8688-3010-5", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2026-06-12T16:08:34Z", "timestamp": 1781280514673, "version": "3.54.1"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]]}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]], "date-time": "2026-02-02T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1769990400000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The growing complexity of modern network infrastructures demands automation solutions that are not limited to the static scripting and traditional Software-Defined Networking (SDN) controllers. In this paper, a new, decentralized, Agentic AI, model of network engineering is presented, designed to provide intent-aware auto-remediation and active optimization. The proposed system makes use of a set of specialized autonomous agents, powered by Local Large Language Models (LLMs) and anchored by Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to read higher-level human intentions, validate them, and implement amendments. The paper introduces a strong Human-in-the-Loop architecture where the critical actions are first checked by a network simulation engine (Batfish) [2] and then approved by operators before being deployed. Its implementation, tested in resource-constrained environments, shows a feasible path towards the implementation of \"NetDevOps\" by integrating a Source of Truth (NetBox), Observability (Prometheus [6] / Loki), and Workflow Orchestration (n8n). The experimental findings validate the fact that the system can convert intent in natural language into valid network configurations that can support agent response times of less than 15ms and hence agility and reliability in network operations.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.36227/techrxiv.177004277.71795055/v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]], "date-time": "2026-02-02T14:32:56Z", "timestamp": 1770042776000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["\"The Era of AI Agents for Network Engineering\": Intent-Aware Auto Remediation for Network Disruption or Failures Using AI Agents, Large Language Models (LLM) and Model Context Protocol (MCP) Mechanisms"], "prefix": "10.36227", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1888-7646", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Oghenekeno Hilkiah", "family": "Okula", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Faculty Of Computing, Engineering and The Built Environment, Birmingham City University (BCU)"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "263", "link": [{"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/pdf/10.36227/techrxiv.177004277.71795055/v1", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2026-06-12T15:48:22Z", "timestamp": 1781279302000}, "score": 41.533726, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/full/10.36227/techrxiv.177004277.71795055/v1"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.177004277.71795055/v1", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}], "items-per-page": 10, "query": {"start-index": 0, "search-terms": null}}}